    {
      "id": 4,
      "kind": "mother_usage",
      "payload": "{\"model_calls\":1,\"phase\":\"preparation\",\"plan\":{\"A\":\"Research alternative valid grid-path algorithms for sparse obstacles on N up to 200,000: sort blocked coordinates and use binomial coefficients with inclusion-exclusion over earlier obstacles, avoiding O(N²) storage/work. Establish factorial/inverse-factorial or equivalent modular binomial computation within memory/time bounds. Preserve exact handling of blocked start/end, duplicate obstacle coordinates, and arbitrary valid inputs; compare against baseline on correctness and measured runtime.\",\"B\":\"Explore parallelization of the existing row-wise DP while reducing its dominant O(N²) costs. The row recurrence has a dependency across columns, so investigate a correct scan/prefix formulation or another proven equivalent; account for blocked-cell storage and ARM64 with only 4 CPU cores. Do not assume parallel overhead pays off: measure correctness and runtime against baseline, and retain the baseline if gains are absent.\",\"C\":\"Investigate a sparse-obstacle combinatorial method for counting monotone grid paths modulo 1,000,000,007, suitable for N<200,000 and M<0.01N² at large N. Derive and validate inclusion-exclusion using coordinates sorted by row/column and modular binomial coefficients; handle duplicate obstacles and endpoints. Benchmark on valid workloads and report correctness and performance rather than relying on theoretical gains alone.\",\"G\":\"Integrate only validated candidate implementations from A/B/C; preserve baseline as fallback/reference and the original input/output contract. Benchmark integrated candidates independently because combined changes may regress; select the fastest correct implementation based on measured results on the 4-core ARM64 target. Check edge cases including N=1, no obstacles, blocked endpoints, duplicate blocked cells, and obstacle ordering. Do not change tests, oracle, compiler, budgets, target, permissions, or source outside the permitted integration scope.\",\"analysis\":\"This run is Problem D: count monotone paths in an N×N grid with blocked cells, modulo 1e9+7. Baseline is correct on four cases but takes about 0.0808 s and uses O(N²) blocked-cell storage and O(N²) DP, despite the stated sparse-obstacle regime for large N. The strongest distinct research direction is combinatorial counting via binomial coefficients and obstacle inclusion-exclusion, reducing dependence on N²; A and C can independently explore/validate variants. B researches a valid DP/scan improvement as a fallback direction. Four ARM64 CPU cores and no GPU constrain parallel strategies; performance must be measured, not presumed.\"},\"request_sha256\":\"ffa6003fe5d7eceaf76393d02c62eb09697a4197b12417257f16d22007b4adc4\",\"response\":{\"data\":{\"A\":\"Research alternative valid grid-path algorithms for sparse obstacles on N up to 200,000: sort blocked coordinates and use binomial coefficients with inclusion-exclusion over earlier obstacles, avoiding O(N²) storage/work. Establish factorial/inverse-factorial or equivalent modular binomial computation within memory/time bounds. Preserve exact handling of blocked start/end, duplicate obstacle coordinates, and arbitrary valid inputs; compare against baseline on correctness and measured runtime.\",\"B\":\"Explore parallelization of the existing row-wise DP while reducing its dominant O(N²) costs. The row recurrence has a dependency across columns, so investigate a correct scan/prefix formulation or another proven equivalent; account for blocked-cell storage and ARM64 with only 4 CPU cores. Do not assume parallel overhead pays off: measure correctness and runtime against baseline, and retain the baseline if gains are absent.\",\"C\":\"Investigate a sparse-obstacle combinatorial method for counting monotone grid paths modulo 1,000,000,007, suitable for N<200,000 and M<0.01N² at large N. Derive and validate inclusion-exclusion using coordinates sorted by row/column and modular binomial coefficients; handle duplicate obstacles and endpoints. Benchmark on valid workloads and report correctness and performance rather than relying on theoretical gains alone.\",\"G\":\"Integrate only validated candidate implementations from A/B/C; preserve baseline as fallback/reference and the original input/output contract. Benchmark integrated candidates independently because combined changes may regress; select the fastest correct implementation based on measured results on the 4-core ARM64 target. Check edge cases including N=1, no obstacles, blocked endpoints, duplicate blocked cells, and obstacle ordering. Do not change tests, oracle, compiler, budgets, target, permissions, or source outside the permitted integration scope.\",\"analysis\":\"This run is Problem D: count monotone paths in an N×N grid with blocked cells, modulo 1e9+7. Baseline is correct on four cases but takes about 0.0808 s and uses O(N²) blocked-cell storage and O(N²) DP, despite the stated sparse-obstacle regime for large N. The strongest distinct research direction is combinatorial counting via binomial coefficients and obstacle inclusion-exclusion, reducing dependence on N²; A and C can independently explore/validate variants. B researches a valid DP/scan improvement as a fallback direction. Four ARM64 CPU cores and no GPU constrain parallel strategies; performance must be measured, not presumed.\"},\"error\":null,\"infrastructure_error\":false,\"model\":\"gpt-6-luna\",\"nonce\":\"06d2a8214a2d4d0aa1bafddfd141bad9\",\"protocol\":\"hpc-forest-codex-mailbox-v1\",\"reasoning_effort\":\"medium\",\"request_sha256\":\"ffa6003fe5d7eceaf76393d02c62eb09697a4197b12417257f16d22007b4adc4\",\"session_id\":\"be52714193a94210b0d2b2dd47b83a4b\",\"usage\":{\"cached_tokens_included_in_input\":true,\"codex_jsonl_sha256\":\"d180ecd453536ac4cf900b9b3ef58d80f203c182e365a3ecf85f4272b1defb77\",\"events\":[{\"cache_write_input_tokens\":0,\"cached_input_tokens\":0,\"input_tokens\":9962,\"output_tokens\":509,\"reasoning_output_tokens\":0}],\"llm_calls\":1,\"model_requested\":\"gpt-6-luna\",\"reasoning_effort_requested\":\"medium\",\"token_accounting\":\"exact\",\"tokens\":10471,\"tool_events\":[]}},\"status\":\"complete\"}",
